markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Tuning a Confidence Threshold

A **confidence threshold** is the line a classifier uses to decide: above it, predict toxic; below it, predict not toxic. 

Below is a visual simulation of the same 8 berries from the toxic-berry activity, each with a fixed confidence score. Drag the threshold and watch which berries get flagged, and how recall and precision trade off as you move it.

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-2/confidence-threshold-tuner.html"
    width="100%"
    height=1000"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Interactive: adjust a confidence threshold and watch recall and precision change">
  </iframe>
</div>
MARKDOWN
